# UI / Component rules

## Structure

```tsx
import { useState } from 'react';
import type { Profile } from '@/types';

interface VolunteerCardProps {
  profile: Profile;
  onSelect?: (id: string) => void;
}

function VolunteerCard({ profile, onSelect }: VolunteerCardProps) {
  // hooks first
  const [isExpanded, setIsExpanded] = useState(false);

  // handlers
  const handleClick = () => {
    onSelect?.(profile.id);
  };

  // render
  return (
    <div className="rounded-lg border p-4 hover:bg-gray-50">
      {/* ... */}
    </div>
  );
}

export default VolunteerCard;
```

## Tailwind

- Mobile-first: write base classes for mobile, use `sm:`, `md:`, `lg:` for larger
- Common spacing: `p-4`, `gap-4`, `space-y-4`
- Use semantic colors via Tailwind: `text-gray-900` for body, `text-gray-600` for secondary, `text-red-600` for errors
- Buttons: use a shared `<Button>` component, not raw `<button>` with classes everywhere
- Cards: `rounded-lg border bg-white p-4 shadow-sm`

## Async UI

Every page/component that fetches data must handle four states:

```tsx
const { data, isLoading, error } = useQuery(...);

if (isLoading) return <Spinner />;
if (error) return <ErrorState error={error} />;
if (!data || data.length === 0) return <EmptyState />;
return <ActualContent data={data} />;
```

## Forms

Use React Hook Form + Zod. Pattern:

```tsx
import { useForm } from 'react-hook-form';
import { zodResolver } from '@hookform/resolvers/zod';
import { z } from 'zod';

const schema = z.object({
  eventName: z.string().min(1, 'Event name is required'),
  eventDate: z.string().min(1),
  signInTime: z.string().min(1),
  signOutTime: z.string().min(1),
}).refine(
  (d) => new Date(d.signOutTime) > new Date(d.signInTime),
  { message: 'Sign-out must be after sign-in', path: ['signOutTime'] }
);

type FormData = z.infer<typeof schema>;

function LogHoursForm() {
  const { register, handleSubmit, formState: { errors, isSubmitting } } =
    useForm<FormData>({ resolver: zodResolver(schema) });

  const onSubmit = async (values: FormData) => {
    // call api function
  };

  return <form onSubmit={handleSubmit(onSubmit)}>...</form>;
}
```

## Accessibility

- All inputs must have associated `<label>` elements
- Buttons must have visible text or `aria-label`
- Color is never the only indicator (icons + text for status)
- Tap targets at least 44×44px on mobile
